+   --  On a 32-bit target whose C library has a 64-bit time_t (musl >= 1.2),
+   --  struct timespec and struct timeval are 16 bytes: the 32-bit
+   --  nanosecond/microsecond field is followed (little endian) by 4 bytes of
+   --  padding, and the library writes the whole structure.  Declare the
+   --  sub-second field as wide as time_t so the Ada record is the same size.
+   --  (Little endian only.)
